 "_README": "Pet level economics. NOT from the game client - the client contains no pet level of any kind. Filled in from the community spreadsheet named in `source`, and the app labels every number it draws from this file as not-from-the-files wherever it shows it.\n\nWHY THIS TABLE AND NOT AN ARBITRARY ONE: its endpoints reconcile exactly with pets.xml. The client states Heal as MaxHeal min=\"10\" max=\"90\" with Cooldown min=\"10\" max=\"1\", and MagicHeal as MaxHeal min=\"1\" max=\"45\" with the same cooldown. This table's level 1 and level 100 rows are 10 every 10s and 90 every 1s, and 1 every 10s and 45 every 1s. Both ends of both abilities, exactly. That also settles the level domain the client never states: 1 to 100.\n\nONE REPAIR, and it is derived from the sheet rather than invented: at level 37 the accumulative cell repeats level 36's value in all three ability tracks. The per-level column is fine and level 38 reconciles against the REPAIRED total (accum38 - perLevel38 = accum36 + perLevel37), not against the printed one - so the cell slipped and the chain above and below it is sound. See `_repairs`.\n\nSHAPE\n  source        a sentence naming where these came from. Blank = the file is ignored.\n  maxLevel      rarity -> highest level. EMPTY: neither the sheet nor the client has it.\n  feedToLevel   [level, cumulative feed power] for the FIRST ability - the default.\n  feedToLevelBy first / second / third - the same per ability slot; later slots cost more.\n  abilityLevels per ability, per level: [level, amount, delay seconds, per second,\n                stat-equivalent]. Stat-equivalent is the sheet's own column: what that\n                rate is worth in Vitality (Heal) or Wisdom (Magic Heal).",
